        "body": "### Summary\n\nFixes #1584.\n\nIn `serveStatic`, `idSearchPaths` previously concatenated `${id}${suffix}` directly.\n- For root requests (`GET /`, where `withoutTrailingSlash` normalizes `id` to `\"/\"`), the default `indexNames: [\"/index.html\"]`, produced `\"//index.html\"`. Looking up `\"//index.html\"` in backends keyed by canonical paths fails and returns 404.\n- For applications configuring relative index names (e.g. `indexNames: [\"index.html\"]`), subfolder lookups like `GET /docs` produced `\"/docsindex.html\"` due to the missing slash.\n\n### Solution\n\nNormalize the join between `id` and `suffix` in `idSearchPaths`: strip leading slashes from `suffix` when non-empty, and join with a single slash boundary (`/${cleanSuffix}` when `id === \"/\"`, or `${id}/${cleanSuffix}` otherwise).\n\n### Tests\n\n- Added tests in `test/static.test.ts` verifying root lookup with default index names returns `/index.html` without double slashes, and relative index names on subfolders resolve correctly to `/sub-static/docs/index.html`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Fixed static file index path resolution so leading slashes in index names do not create malformed paths. Relative index names now resolve correctly at the root and in nested folders.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
